Please state the real scenarios. The client (`attestation_tdx`) calls
symbols exported by `tdx_guest`, so the module dependency forces `tdx_guest` to be
initialized before the client can even load, and prevents `tdx_guest` from
being unloaded while the client is loaded. The "attach at init" and
"driver removal calls the client's remove callback" cases are therefore only
reachable with both built in (init-order), and never at removal. The text
suggests more generality than exists.

> +available.  Otherwise attachment occurs when the TDX guest driver finishes
> +initialization.  Driver removal calls the client's remove callback before
> +freeing report or Quote buffers.  Client unregistration similarly drains the
> +attachment before returning.
> +
> +The misc ioctl, TSM-report configfs interface, and TSM-MR sysfs attributes
> +remain independent frontends over the same native serialization and buffers.
