Summary of the most serious issues:

 - TSM report path regression: always `kvmalloc()`s `TDX_QUOTE_MAX_LEN`
   (~128 KiB) per report instead of an exact-size copy.
 - A failing in-kernel client attach at init now fails the whole
   `tdx_guest` module init, killing the misc/TSM interfaces the commit message
   says are preserved.
 - Exit-path detach and `tdx_service_ready` handling are unreachable given the
   module symbol dependency; the documentation overstates the lifecycle.
 - Constants duplicated in the new public header with `static_asserts` instead
   of sharing the uapi definitions; `struct device` *dev parameter on every
   op is speculative generality; magic number 4 for RTMRs.
 - Unrelated MAINTAINERS additions not in the commit message.
 - `mr_read` does a full TDCALL per call and discards most of it; kernel-doc
   lacks the size/locking/context contract.
